id: ops-zq8c
title: Include TSX in docstring and duplication gates with verified source counts
description: "GitHub #128: pm-ops docstring and duplication gates silently omit TSX sources. Make both engines scan TSX, prove source-count completeness, and certify the exact package head."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:quality",docstrings,duplication,tsx
created_at: "2026-09-28T15:05:31.893Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T15:18:38.784Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Directory and single-file docstring analysis find undocumented TSX exports; jscpd 4 and 5 detect TSX clones with the real engines; mismatched scan counts fail closed; release gate passes; companion records exact limitations.
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T15:05:31.893Z",codex,"TDD: TSX docstring and real jscpd 4 tests failed before the source fix. The candidate passes 449/451 tests with two existing opt-in skips, c8 100/100/100/100, 221/221 documented declarations, zero duplication across 43 sources, zero production audit findings, and real packed npm/Node and Bun TSX acceptance. The local PM CLI SDK pin is 2026.9.28."
  "2026-09-28T15:18:38.784Z",codex,"PR #132 first-head review found two valid regressions. Greptile P1 reproduced: a JSX closing tag let the tokenizer hide a later export; the TSX scanner now uses LanguageVariant.JSX and focused tests cover both direct analysis and directory walking. CodeRabbit major reproduced: fast-glob followed symlinked paths while jscpd 5 did not; fast-glob and jscpd 4 now share the no-symlink policy with jscpd 5, with real 4/5 symlink fixtures. Focused tests, build, typecheck, lint, and docstrings pass; full exact-head gate and packed acceptance remain pending."
